# What `gcloud builds submit .` uploads. Never ship secrets, data or local outputs.
.git
.gitignore
# google-github-actions/auth writes its credential config into the WORKSPACE ROOT, which is
# exactly the directory `builds submit .` tarballs up -- so without this line it is uploaded to
# the staging bucket on every CI deploy. Verified by unpacking the tarball, not assumed. It holds
# no long-lived key (that is the point of WIF), but credential_source.headers carries the live
# Actions bearer token, which can mint OIDC tokens for our provider while the job runs.
# `*credentials*.json` in .gitignore does NOT match it: the file is named "creds", not
# "credentials". This also keeps the CI checkout clean, so deploy.sh stops tagging images
# "<sha>-dirty" -- a mutable tag that silently breaks rollback-by-tag.
gha-creds-*.json
gha-oidc-*
.env
.env.*
infra/env.sh
docs/
data/
runs/
**/node_modules/
web/dist/
**/__pycache__/
.venv/
*.tif
*.npy
*.mp4
*.mov
